                },
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "XuPWT",
                  "name": "Browse masters",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "gap": 20,
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "frame",
                      "id": "qF9a4",
                      "name": "cmp/ChatBrowseTick",
                      "context": "One tick = one user message, in conversation order.\n\nLength is NOT data — it is proximity to the pointer. At rest every tick is the same 10; as the pointer moves down the rail each tick grows toward 26 on a raised-cosine falloff over 4 neighbours, so the rail reads as a lens tracking the cursor. Ticks grow along X only: their y never moves, so the row you are aiming at cannot slip out from under you while the lens swells.\n\nHeight $tick-h (2), radius 1. tick axis: default (fg.subtle, at rest or outside the lens) | hover (fg.muted, inside the lens) | active (fg, the tick under the pointer — the one the ChatBrowseCard is showing). Colour and length fall off together. Everything returns to default/10 when the pointer leaves the rail.",
                      "theme": {
                        "tick": "default"
                      },
                      "reusable": true,
                      "width": 18,
                      "height": 2,
                      "fill": "$tick-fill",
                      "cornerRadius": 1
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "frame",
                      "id": "O4EJB2",
                      "name": "cmp/ChatBrowseCard",
                      "context": "Hover preview for a ChatBrowse tick. Shows the turn the tick indexes: the user Message (fg, the thing you are aiming for) over a muted Reply preview that identifies which turn it was — the message alone is often not enough to tell two similar asks apart.\n\nBoth lines are clamped to 2 lines and ellipsized; the card is a fixed 320 so the rail does not jitter as you move down it. Opens on hover of a tick and follows that tick's y, clamped inside the panel. Reply is optional — hide it for a turn the agent has not answered yet.",
                      "reusable": true,
                      "width": 320,
                      "fill": "$ds-elevated",
                      "cornerRadius": 10,
                      "stroke": "$ds-border",
                      "strokeWidth": 1,
                      "strokeAlignment": "inner",
                      "layout": "vertical",
                      "gap": 7,
                      "padding": 12,
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "id": "TrZkC",
                          "name": "Message",
                          "fill": "$ds-fg",
                          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                          "width": "fill_container",
