                    {
                      "type": "frame",
                      "id": "yA7dV",
                      "name": "cmp/ChatToolRow",
                      "context": "One collapsed tool call in an assistant turn. Rows stack flush — the row is exactly its content height and the group adds no gap between rows — so a run of calls reads as one quiet block instead of a list of separate entries. Separation belongs to the group boundary: the stack takes extra space above (8) to detach it from whatever precedes it; never reintroduce per-row spacing.\n\nThe icon is bare: no ring, no plate. A 20px outlined disc around every glyph turned a quiet list of calls into a column of buttons competing with the assistant's text; the glyph alone is enough to type the row.\n\ncall axis: rest | hover. The chevron exists only while the row is hovered (call: hover) or while the call is expanded — at rest the row is glyph + label + argument and nothing else. A column of permanent chevrons repeats the same affordance once per row; showing it on the row under the pointer says the same thing exactly when it is needed. When it does appear, it sits immediately after the label, not flushed right — it is the affordance for THIS row's disclosure, so it belongs with the thing it opens.\n\nThe trailing slot is the ONE thing worth reading without expanding: Lk (the file, info-coloured) OR St (a bare status) OR Diff (+/− counts). Enable exactly one; two competing arguments defeat the point of collapsing.\n\ntool axis: ok | error. Error recolours the glyph only ($ds-error) and swaps it for triangle-alert — the label stays fg.muted so a failed call does not shout louder than the prose around it.",
                      "theme": {
                        "tool": "ok"
                      },
                      "reusable": true,
                      "width": 420,
                      "gap": 8,
                      "alignItems": "center",
