            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "B2H8jV",
              "name": "Kanban renderer",
              "context": "The collection renderer, drawn as a kanban. One renderer draws a whole resource set in two displays — a detailed list (tree: groups collapse, rows indent, attributes ride right as chips) and a kanban board (groups become columns, rows become draggable cards). Display is a setting on the renderer, not a mode of the workbench.\n\nTwo parts: a header (cmp/ViewBar) naming the saved views and holding the Filter and Display menus, and the body, which is the display. A view is a NAME over a (filter + display) pair, so switching a tab can change both which resources are present and whether they are rows or cards. At rest the filter clauses live inside the Filter modal, not the header; editing a filter or display detaches the active view, marks its tab, and drops in a subheader listing the applied clauses with Reset / Save.\n\nFull spec and both displays: the 'Kanban Renderer · Component' frame.",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "height": 865,
              "fill": "$ds-bg-subtle",
              "cornerRadius": 12,
              "stroke": "$ds-border",
