                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "ZK4tI",
                  "name": "Patterns / Kanban Renderer / Create Dialog",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "fill": "$ds-bg-subtle",
                  "cornerRadius": 12,
                  "stroke": "$ds-border",
                  "strokeWidth": 1,
                  "strokeAlignment": "inner",
                  "layout": "vertical",
                  "padding": [
                    28,
                    0
                  ],
                  "alignItems": "center",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "frame",
                      "id": "vmzs5",
                      "name": "cmp/ResourceCreateDialog",
                      "context": "The shared create dialog. Every control in it is declared rather than hand-built, and the host renders the whole surface — there is no extension webview here.\n\nTwo zones, two sources.\n\nPROPERTIES are derived. They are the resource's own editable attributes, already declared once by the renderer's attribute schema and delivered live with every query. Nothing re-declares them: the form filters on editable and seeds whichever attribute the board groups by from the selected column. Add a tag to the project and the form grows a selector on its own.\n\nCONTENT is declared. The create contribution names its typed params — markdown, text, number, boolean, files — and each type maps to exactly one @pstdio/ui control. When an extension needs a control the vocabulary lacks, the answer is to add the type, here and in the component library, the same way a visual the recipes cannot express means a recipe is missing. The vocabulary is the design system's form surface enumerated; it is not a per-extension escape hatch.\n\nThis is a form, and forms are declarable. Rich per-resource editing is a different surface — the resource editor view — and that one stays a webview.\n\nThree things to hold: status appears once, as the first control under Properties, disabled because the column already chose it. The attach affordance sits under the field it applies to, so the footer stays a pure commit bar. And all copy, chrome included, arrives as Localizable — the dialog ships no English of its own.",
                      "reusable": true,
                      "clip": true,
                      "width": 600,
                      "height": 424,
                      "fill": "$ds-bg",
                      "cornerRadius": "$overlay-radius",
                      "stroke": "$ds-border",
                      "strokeWidth": 1,
                      "strokeAlignment": "inner",
                      "layout": "vertical",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "type": "frame",
                          "id": "KQyfR",
                          "name": "Header",
                          "width": "fill_container",
                          "height": 52,
                          "stroke": "$ds-border-subtle",
