                          "name": "Note",
                          "fill": "$ds-fg-muted",
                          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                          "width": "fill_container",
                          "content": "One tick per user message, in order — the rail is how you scan and jump through a long session. Tick length is proximity to the pointer, not data: the ticks nearest the cursor swell into a lens, which is what makes a 2px target hittable. They grow along X only, so the row you are aiming at never moves out from under you. Colour and length fall off together.",
