            {
              "type": "text",
              "id": "KJTwY",
              "name": "Sub",
              "fill": "$ds-fg-muted",
              "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
              "width": 1240,
              "content": "Today an extension is a row: a name, a version, a switch, a trash can. But the row is the smallest thing we know about it and the largest thing we show. An extension declares commands, modes, panels, skills and settings of its own — and it can fail. None of that fits on a row, and none of it earns a mode: extensions are managed, not selected. So the page lives where the list already lives, one level deeper in the settings overlay, and answers the only two questions worth asking — what did this add to my workbench, and what can I change.",
              "lineHeight": 1.5,
              "fontFamily": "$font-body",
              "fontSize": 16,
              "fontWeight": "normal"
            }
