                  "name": "D",
                  "fill": "$ds-fg-muted",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "The same view, the same filters, the same ten resources — re-laid out. The group that was a header row is a column, the row is a card, and the status change that was a menu in the list is a drag here. Nothing the list showed is lost: id, labels, date and assignee ride on the card, and state is carried once by the column it sits in rather than repeated on every card. Because display belongs to the view and the display just changed, the tab is marked and the Filters subheader drops in — this arrangement is unsaved until you Save it.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.45,
                  "fontFamily": "$font-body",
                  "fontSize": 12,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
