                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "NxsyQ",
                  "name": "D",
                  "fill": "$ds-fg-muted",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "A view names a pair: the filter that narrows the set and the display that draws it. That is why switching to a saved view can change both which rows are present and whether they are rows at all. The header carries the names, not the clauses — open Filter or Display to see what the active view actually is, and to change it. Editing either detaches the view and raises Reset / Save.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.45,
                  "fontFamily": "$font-body",
                  "fontSize": 12,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
