                  "content": "Panel anatomy",
                  "fontFamily": "$font-heading",
                  "fontSize": 16,
                  "fontWeight": "600"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "dSdDY",
                  "name": "D",
                  "fill": "$ds-fg-muted",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": 1300,
                  "content": "Tabs and the “+” sit on the left of the strip. Attached panel menus default to 280px and have no internal header or close action; they collapse by dragging the divider closed. Closed menus use directional panel-open icons instead of their content icons, and open as dropdowns where a single icon button reattaches them. The visible dropdown surface anchors directly below its own icon.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.45,
                  "fontFamily": "$font-body",
                  "fontSize": 12,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "L5Ul0",
                  "name": "N",
                  "fill": "$ds-fg-subtle",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": 1300,
                  "content": "The menus belong to the panel, not the slot — bubblify the session into a floating panel and Context files goes with it, icon and all. This is also the reason the sidenav needs a resource region: navigating a workspace's children is not a panel action, so no panel menu can own it.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.45,
                  "fontFamily": "$font-body",
                  "fontSize": 11,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
